    {
      "id": "decl-invariants",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Invariants",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": -640
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Invariants",
        "body": "**What makes this thing a root, specifically?**\n\n- Exactly one root per graph (a fragment may have none; it never has two).\n- Owns `data.identity` — `graphId`, `name`, `version`, `description` — for the graph as a whole. A graph is named here and nowhere else.\n- Owns `data.intent` — `kind` and `scope` — stating what kind of artifact this graph is.\n- Is reachable as the graph's implicit root Port even when no other node explicitly claims that role.\n- Every other node that belongs to this graph shares its `graphId`.\n\nEvery Surface has a face before its terminal Glyph. Rendering glyph-shaped artwork does not require a face named Icon.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592052362,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
