    {
      "id": "decl-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "**What data belongs to it?**\n\n```text\nidentity      { graphId, name, version, description }\nintent        { kind, scope }\nroot          { kind, defaultSurfaceId, surfaces[] }\nmembrane      { bounds, … }   the graph's boundary (see Membrane)\nauthority     { mutation{allowCreate,allowUpdate,allowDelete}, actors{humans,agents,tools} }\nsettings      { layout, autoSave }\ndocument      { url }\n```\n\nRequired at minimum: `identity.graphId`, `identity.name`, `identity.version`, `identity.description`, `intent.kind`, `intent.scope`, `root.kind`.\n\nA file's `metadata` keeps only its dates, author, tags and preferred viewer. The graph's name, description, id and version are on the root's `identity`, never in `metadata`.\n\nGitHub repository, path and branch are not part of the root. They live in the file's own top-level `settings.github`, one level above any node, where the commit flow reads them.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592052363,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
