    {
      "id": "decl-behavior",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Behavior",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 440
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Behavior",
        "body": "## Agreed semantics\n\nThe root supplies artifact identity, exposure and authority. It has no independent program that runs merely because the node exists. Consumers use its contract for navigation, validation, presentation and save ownership. The graph-facing Surface chains and the root node's own class presentation have separate owners.\n\nThe relationship grammar, defaults and validator read Surface chains. Navigation uses exposed Ports and the ground. The root node still has a dedicated rendering fallback (`ManifestNode`); the template/class path is not universally substituted. A pinned ground is drawn beneath the graph's edges and other nodes, and is not lifted over them when selected. A document has no ground: its page is its first face, drawn across the graph.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
