      "showLabel": false
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-boundary",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
        "body": "- The root does not render content. Rendering the graph's actual material is the job of faces and Content; the root only names which node fills each presentation role.\n- The root does not own node positions or layout. Where nodes sit on the canvas is unrelated to identity.\n- The root does not define *how* an exposed face looks — only *which* node is assigned to that role.\n- The root does not grant runtime capability beyond what `authority` explicitly states. Absence of a grant means the action is not permitted, not that it's merely undocumented.\n- A root is not a template. It describes one graph's own identity, not a reusable composition pattern for building other graphs (see Templates).\n- The root does not vouch for which custom node types are safe to use in the graph. That authority comes from the graph's imports, each reaching a real class definition.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592052366,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "side": "top",
          "offset": 0.2,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": false,
      "resizable": true,
      "portPosition": "center",
      "showLabel": false
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-examples",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Examples",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 440
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Examples",
        "body": "**Examples live outside the primitive, referenced, not embedded.**\n\n**Weekend Reading Group** is a small plan graph whose root is bound to a custom class (still named Custom Declaration), allowed to use it by an import, drawn as a card that shows its own name, kind and version, and edited with the complete form. It has one Surface (a plan, a summary, an icon, then a glyph) and a landing page as its ground, and it is laid out the way its template teaches. Open it with the portal beside this node.\n\nThat template is the other reference: a page that explains each part of a root and walks through building one.\n\nNo canon graph has a custom root yet; the example linked here is still in a personal library, under its old name (`templates/declaration-template`).",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592052367,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
